# Local Python environments and caches
hls/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Generated HLS/Vivado output
hls/*/*/solution1/
# `logs/*` rather than `logs/`: git will not descend into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so a later `!logs/<name>/` negation on a plain `logs/` rule can
# never take effect.  Excluding the contents instead leaves the directory
# traversable, which is what makes the Priority 4 exceptions at the bottom of
# this file work.
logs/*
*.rpt
*.jou

# Batch/debug outputs
batch_out*/

# Binary/generated archives and test vectors
*.bin
*.zip

# Vitis HLS/XSim transient output
hls/**/*.log
hls/**/*.pb
hls/**/*.wdb
hls/**/xsim.dir/
hls/**/dfx_runtime.txt
hls/integration/pe_tme_seam/

# Deterministic integration manifests
hls/integration/tb_*_tme_cases.txt

# EXCEPTION: gate 4's eight fixtures ARE committed (~0.56 MB total).
# board_gate_extract.py is the extractor's board gate and it is worthless
# without the exact bytes it was written against: regenerating them on the
# board would make the gate agree with whatever it had just produced, and a
# result that cannot be tied to specific bytes is not a result. They are
# deterministic (the generators self-check against pinned SHA-256) and
# derived from nothing confidential. Their hashes live in
# sw/GATE4_VECTORS.sha256 and the gate refuses to run on a mismatch.
# Everything else generated stays ignored.
!hls/integration/tb_bpe_tme_cases.txt
!hls/integration/tb_bpe_tme_gray.bin
!hls/integration/tb_bpe_tme_bin.bin
!hls/integration/tb_bpe_tme_patch.bin
!hls/integration/tb_bpe_tme_templs.bin
!hls/template_match/tb_tme_cases_hw.txt
!hls/template_match/tb_tme_patches_hw.bin
!hls/template_match/tb_tme_templs_hw.bin

# EXCEPTION: gate 5's five fixtures, on the same argument and at 16 KB.
# board_gate_protocol.py is the multi-candidate stream-protocol gate and it is
# equally worthless without the exact bytes. Hashes in sw/GATE5_VECTORS.sha256.
!hls/integration/tb_proto_cases.txt
!hls/integration/tb_proto_gray.bin
!hls/integration/tb_proto_bin.bin
!hls/integration/tb_proto_patches.bin
!hls/integration/tb_proto_templs.bin

# NOT an exception: the production-geometry vector package is ~1.6 MB and
# stays out. It is fully determined by the pinned seeds in
# tme_generate_production.py, so `sha256sum -c tb_tme_prod.sha256` after a
# regeneration is stronger evidence than a committed copy would be — it proves
# the generator still produces the vectors that were verified, rather than
# proving a file was not edited. The RECORD is committed; the payload is not.
hls/template_match/tb_tme_cases_prod.txt
hls/template_match/tb_tme_counts_prod.txt
!hls/template_match/tb_tme_prod.sha256

# Same treatment for the Priority 4 (B1) banking-boundary suite, and for the
# same reason: it is fully determined by the pinned seeds in
# tme_generate_production.py, so `sha256sum -c tb_tme_b1.sha256` after
# `--suite b1` proves the generator still makes the vectors that were verified.
# Committing 44 KB of payload would only prove a file was not edited.
hls/template_match/tb_tme_cases_b1.txt
!hls/template_match/tb_tme_b1.sha256

# Confidential-derived detector output. The per-page detection dumps carry
# pin labels read off the drawings; only the aggregate manifest and its
# provenance file may be committed (see sw/cpu_baseline_snapshot.py, which
# also refuses to write dumps inside the repo).
*_detections.json
baseline_cpu_*/

# EXCEPTION: the Priority 4 (B1) evidence set, ~7.1 MB, listed artifact by
# artifact in logs/b1_20260818/MANIFEST.sha256 and verified by
# `python sw/tme_b1_manifest.py --verify`.
#
# The rules above ignore `logs/`, `*.rpt` and `*.zip`, which is right for build
# noise and wrong for this: a manifest over files a clean checkout does not
# contain is a local checksum, not evidence. Commit 0373859 carried none of it.
# The general policy — commit the RECORD, regenerate the payload — does not
# apply either, because these artifacts are NOT regenerable. The bitstream is
# built from a Vivado block design that lives outside this repository
# (C:/Users/lychee/tc25/vivado_project/), the board transcripts record a session
# that happened once, and a co-simulation report cannot be re-derived from
# anything committed here in under half an hour of tool time.
#
# `sw/tme_b1_manifest.py --mirror` is what copies these in from the build tree;
# nothing here is edited in place.
!logs/b1_20260818/
!logs/b1_20260818/**
!logs/b1_board_20260818/
!logs/b1_board_20260818/**
!logs/b1_rerun_20260818/
!logs/b1_rerun_20260818/**
!logs/scale_policy_20260818/
!logs/scale_policy_20260818/**

# The Priority 5 (B2) evidence set, on exactly the same argument: it is bound by
# logs/b2_20260819/MANIFEST.sha256 and verified by
# `python sw/tme_b2_manifest.py --verify`, and a manifest over files a clean
# checkout does not contain is a local checksum rather than evidence. It also
# carries tme_cycle_model.py.pre_b2, WITHOUT WHICH `tme_b2_ab.py --predict`
# cannot run at all: that mode reads the pre-measurement model deliberately, so
# that the withdrawn projection cannot be quietly replaced by the answer.
!logs/b2_20260819/
!logs/b2_20260819/**

# The Priority 2 and Priority 3 transcripts, 145 KB, on a narrower argument:
# sw/tme_cycle_model.py --assert RE-READS them to corroborate its frozen
# literals, and in a checkout that lacks them it reports
# "board transcripts (logs/board_125mhz_gate/) ABSENT" and re-derives 2 of 6
# values instead of 6.  A Priority 0 evidence tool that cannot re-prove itself
# from a clone is not doing the job it exists for.
!logs/board_125mhz_gate/
!logs/board_125mhz_gate/**
!logs/tme_125_timing/
!logs/tme_125_timing/**
!logs/phase_s_20260818/
!logs/phase_s_20260818/**
!logs/phase_s_board_20260818/
!logs/phase_s_board_20260818/**
!hls/template_match/template_match_b1*/**/*.rpt
!hls/template_match/template_match_b1/SUPERSEDED.md
!hls/template_match/template_match_b1/b1/impl/ip/component.xml
!hls/template_match/template_match_b1/b1/impl/ip/TermCountB1_hls_tme_top_0_2.zip

# The phase_s board vectors, on the same argument as gate 4's and gate 5's: the
# B1 board session's entire claim to being a CONTROLLED comparison is that the
# runner and these three files did not change between it and the Priority 3
# session. That claim is uncheckable from a clone that does not carry them.
!hls/template_match/tb_tme_cases_phase_s.txt
!hls/template_match/tb_tme_patches_phase_s.bin
!hls/template_match/tb_tme_templs_phase_s.bin
!hls/template_match/tb_tme_phase_s.sha256
